menu "Kernel Workqueue"

config WORKQUEUE_PENDING_CAP
    usize "Per-pool pending work ring capacity"
    range 8 1024
    default 128
    help
      Maximum number of pending work entries one worker pool can hold.
      All logical workqueues attached to a per-CPU pool share this
      bounded ring, so capacity pressure grows with the number of
      attached queues. Enqueue into a full ring fails instead of
      blocking or allocating, keeping the enqueue path IRQ-safe.
      Raising the cap increases static memory usage by one entry slot
      per added slot per pool.

config WORKQUEUE_WORKERS_PER_POOL
    usize "Maximum worker tasks per system worker pool"
    range 1 16
    default 4
    help
      Maximum number of worker tasks one per-CPU system worker pool may
      run. IRQ-safe enqueue paths never create tasks; a per-CPU manager task
      creates workers on demand up to this cap. Raising the cap increases
      per-pool static worker records and worker wake-source storage.

config KFEAT_KWORK_STRESS
    bool "Enable workqueue procfs stress trigger"
    depends on KFEAT_FS
    default n
    help
      Enable /proc/kwork_stress for manually triggered long-running workqueue
      stress cases. This is a diagnostics-only interface and must remain
      disabled in normal builds.

endmenu
